<%# locals: (event:, registration: nil) %>
<%#
  The reader's own row, in the two states that are a question or an answer. A `reserved` registration draws nothing until the event ends: it is a place held before anybody was asked, and the legend reads that absence as the state rather than as a question waiting. Once the event has ended `Registration#asked?` asks it whether they went, together with an invitation nobody answered and a maybe, and the pills are `Event#available_registration_answers`, which leaves the maybe out.

  Nothing is drawn on an event that no longer takes answers, because `Registration` refuses every pill there. No registration draws nothing either, and so does one the policy will not let this reader write.

  Each answer is its own small button, a ghost until chosen; the chosen one is solid in its status colour, which reads on the cards' `base-200` as well as on the page, and the others carry that colour on their icon alone.
%>
<% chosen = { "yes" => "btn-success", "maybe" => "btn-warning", "no" => "btn-error" } %>
<% inks = { "yes" => "text-success", "maybe" => "text-warning", "no" => "text-error" } %>
<% if registration && event.open_to_answers? && (registration.asked? || registration.answered?) && allowed_to?(:update?, registration) %>
  <div class="space-y-1">
    <%# WHY: the buttons sit beside the question while the line has room for both, and wrap below it as one group, 8px down, when it does not. %>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
      <p class="text-sm"><%= registration.asked? ? answer_prompt(event) : "Your answer:" %></p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <% event.available_registration_answers.each do |answer| %>
          <% current = registration.status == answer %>
          <%= button_to group_event_registration_path(event.group, event, registration),
                method: :patch,
                params: { registration: { status: answer } },
                class: "btn btn-sm #{current ? chosen[answer] : "btn-ghost"}",
                aria: (current ? { current: "true" } : {}) do %>
            <%= icon answer, class: "size-3.5 #{inks[answer] unless current}" %>
            <%= answer.capitalize %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <% if registration.invited? %>
      <p class="text-xs">Asked <%= time_ago_in_words(registration.updated_at) %> ago · no answer yet</p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
